  "text": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "The sun is in the window. It is a school day. The sun is big and yellow. May and Pat are in their room. May has a song for Pat. \"Sing with me, Pat,\" says May. \"What song?\" asks Pat. \"The Clothes Song,\" says May.",
      "\"Hat, hat, on my head!\" \"Shirt, shirt, on my body!\" \"Jacket, jacket, on my arms!\" \"Shorts, shorts, on my legs!\" \"Shoes, shoes, on my feet!\" \"Hands, hands, clap, clap, clap!\" \"Smile, smile, I am happy!\" Pat sings the song with May. He points to his head. He points to his feet. They sing it two times.",
      "\"Look at me!\" says Pat. He has a hat and a jacket. His shoes are blue. May claps her hands. Pat is five and May is eight. Mom says, \"Well done, Pat!\" Pat smiles at the sun. \"Can we sing it again?\" he asks. \"Yes, we can!\" says May. Then they go to school."
    ],
    "summary": "May teaches her small brother Pat a clothes song. Pat sings it, puts on his clothes, and smiles at the sun.",
